-- TRIEL example inside the formal core: the reaction of an AI agent that runs
-- a shop to a low-stock alert. It is the companion of merchant_mandate.triel.
--
-- One activation of the specification is one alert: the activation entry is
-- the moment the alert is raised, and every duration counts from it
-- (formal/core/CORE.md, section 8.3, point 5), as in
-- gdpr_art33_notification.triel and sensor_overheat.triel. The agent must
-- prepare a restock within 4 hours of the alert; preparing it exactly at the
-- deadline fulfils the obligation. A missed deadline is a breach, which
-- notifies the owner; NOTIFY is informational, so the obligation stays
-- breached and is closed (section 8.3, point 12), and a restock prepared later
-- changes nothing (low_stock_late_restock). Preparing a restock (stage_restock)
-- and applying it (apply_restock) are different actions: whether the restock
-- is then applied is decided by the prohibitions of merchant_mandate.triel,
-- which read the stock level at the application, under its freshness rule, so
-- a level that was low at the alert may be stale by then and the restock
-- blocked until the owner approves it.
--
-- The invariant states that a stock level is known at some entry within the
-- 4 hours: EVENTUALLY(PRESENT(stock_units)) WITHIN 4 HOURS. In this file
-- stock_units has no MAX_AGE, so PRESENT reads the data as given. Missing data
-- neither fulfil nor violate EVENTUALLY ... WITHIN (convention 11); here the
-- condition is PRESENT, which is always defined (eval_present_defined), so the
-- invariant is T once a stock level is present in time and F once the 4 hours
-- pass without one. F is a statement about the data, not about the stock: a
-- condition with PRESENT is outside the theorems on more data, and adding a
-- level to an entry of the window turns F into T (T3_present_not_monotone).
--
-- An alert raised in the middle of a longer trace is not handled here: inside
-- the core a duration counts from the activation, a deadline inside a branch
-- of IF or WHEN is rejected (formal/core/CORE.md, section 10.6, further
-- rejections), and ON ... DO, which waits for an event, is outside the core;
-- so the host starts one activation per alert. Every construct in this file is
-- translated into the Isabelle/HOL core (formal/core) and evaluated by the
-- exported evaluator (evaluator/).

SPECIFICATION merchant_low_stock VERSION 1.0.0

SUBJECTS {
  owner : PARTY,
  agent : SYSTEM
}

TERMS {
  agent MUST stage_restock WITHIN 4 HOURS;
  agent ON_BREACH NOTIFY owner
}

FACTORS {
  stock_units : Integer METADATA
}

INVARIANTS {
  stock_known : LIVENESS : EVENTUALLY(PRESENT(stock_units)) WITHIN 4 HOURS
}
